hi there steve kaufman here again and  today i'm going to talk about language  immersion  if you enjoy these videos on language  learning please subscribe  and also i remind you that for those of  you who are not native speakers this  video the audio the transcript can be  studied at link and i'm going to leave a  link link  in the description box so you can study  this to improve your english i think we  all know that language immersion  is an ideal way to improve in a language  what do we mean by language immersion  obviously it means being immersed in the  language in other words hearing the  language reading the language speaking  the language being you know covered head  to foot so to speak if we think of the  analogy with swimming or being immersed  in water language immersion is being  immersed in the language now this is  normally it can be the situation if you  live where the language is spoken if you  live surrounded by the language you're  immersed in the language  now being where the language is spoken  is no guarantee  that in others you may in fact be  immersed immersed in the language  potentially you're in a language  immersion situation but don't take  advantage of it and we have many  examples here in canada for example of  immigrants who live here for many years  and don't improve in english because  they don't take advantage of that  environment so it's no guarantee  and and part of the reason why they  don't is because let's face it it's not  that easy you do have to have a strategy  you do have to prepare yourself you  can't just go there and expect somehow  by magic that you're going to pick up  the language when i went to japan i  didn't go to school but i learned japan  and japanese i spent a lot of time  listening and reading and building up my  vocabulary so that i can i could  understand what what people were saying  so that i could interact with them so  you still have to have a strategy even  if you are immersed in the language  now if you are not where the language is  spoken then i think you could have a  kind of a related strategy which is what  i do like right now i'm working on  polish and i would like one day to go to  poland  i hope i do go i don't know when i will  go but i have that as a goal to  eventually put myself in a situation  where i will be immersed i'll be  experiencing language immersion so i  spend a lot of time  reading on the internet i use that link  i use our link chrome extension to  quickly import articles from polish  newspapers  while maintaining my ukrainian and  russian  and i listen and once a week or so i may  speak in other words i'm preparing  myself  with the thought that one day i will be  in that language immersion environment  and i'll be you know ready to hit the  ground running so you do need to have a  strategy whether you're in that  immersion environment or whether you're  trying to create an artificial immersion  environment and and of course that's  much easier to do today than it ever was  in the past  also when i think of language immersion  i think of french immersion  uh here in canada where  anglophone students  study or do most of their in fact all of  their schooling for the first seven  eight nine years in french and then by  grade 10 and 11 it tapers off a bit but  at least half their subjects are in  french even in those final years  and apparently because i have three  grandchildren who went through the  program uh the first six seven years or  so the kids do speak to each other in  french and then they are less and less  inclined to do so so that the immersion  experience becomes less of a full  language immersion experience  also  they read in class but they don't have  any handy tools to make that reading  easier for them and it is hard to read  on science or history or whatever it  might be math in another language so i  think that link  would be very useful in this immersion  environment because it adds another  dimension so they're not just reading  they can listen to the text they can  save words and phrases  and also i think the audio helps give  you some momentum  because i've always especially when i  was younger reading in french as a 17  year old was more difficult but if you  have the audio if you can easily look up  new words and see the words that you  previously looked up and so forth it  just gives you more momentum and makes  it a more complete language immersion  experience in my view anyway those are  my views on language immersion and i  look forward to your thoughts  bye for now
 

